Patient or Clinician?

Software license: MIT (see LICENSE). MIT was chosen because every runtime
dependency (numpy, pandas, scikit-learn: BSD-3-Clause; pytest, dev only: MIT) is
permissive and the viewer has no third-party code or assets (system fonts only).

Data: this repository contains NO data. It analyses the PhysioNet/Computing in
Cardiology Challenge 2019 training data, which users download themselves from
PhysioNet. That dataset has its own license and attribution terms, which are NOT
covered by this repository's MIT license. To our understanding PhysioNet lists it
under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0); this could not be verified from
the build environment -- confirm on the dataset page before redistributing any
derived data. Required citations:

  Reyna MA, et al. Early Prediction of Sepsis From Clinical Data: The
  PhysioNet/Computing in Cardiology Challenge 2019. Crit Care Med 2020;48(2):210-217.
  Goldberger AL, et al. PhysioBank, PhysioToolkit, and PhysioNet. Circulation
  2000;101(23):e215-e220.

Generated files in results/ are derived from that data (aggregate metrics and a
small number of per-patient time series). Review the dataset terms before
publishing results/attribution_cases.json.
